--
--
A second DISTINCT unordered_map::emplace instantiation fails "found
no match for symbol 'emplace'" -- diagnosis 2026-07-22: while
re-instantiating __detail::_Select1st::operator()<_Tp> (via
_Hash_code_base) the partial specializations of its member template
__1st_type fail to rebind their parameters (convert_template_parameter
finds _Tp unbound in an active-deduction map).  Any second argument
shape triggers it, even on a DIFFERENT map type (global, not per-map
state); each call converts fine alone.  A header-free replica of the
_Select1st shape passes -- the full hashtable context is required.
From restrict_function_pointers.cpp's
merge_function_pointer_restrictions; blocks that dog-food TU.
See also cpp17_vector_emplace_nondefault_pair: a SINGLE emplace_back
already fails when the pair has a non-default-constructible member
(constrained-pair-constructor family, [temp.deduct]/8).
More minimal same-root sibling: cpp17_vector_emplace_nondefault_pair
(deduced heterogeneous parameter pack homogenized to its first
element in the member-template instance signature).
Minimal header-free reproducer: cpp17_hashtable_alias_default_arg.
